      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'CONCLUSION


    From this experiment, we hereby conclude that Mohr''s
    salt is a double salt of ammonium sulphate and ferrous sulphate.


    The formula
    of Mohr''s salt is (NH4)2Fe(SO4)2.6H2O.


    The preparation of Mohr''s salt
    includes mixing both salts in the same equimolar ratio in water and dilute sulphuric
    acid, followed by boiling and cooling to form crystals.


    The shape of the
    crystal is monoclinic.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
